{"id":"753698ebb6dab618","group":"27","path":"27/27-thm-dualtransversal.md","title":"Dual prime implicants as minimal literal transversals","display":"thm-dualtransversal — Dual prime implicants as minimal literal transversals","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Boolean Functions: Theory, Algorithms, and Applications","book_abbrev":"27","label":"27-thm-dualtransversal","aliases":["27-thm-dualtransversal"],"display":"thm-dualtransversal — Dual prime implicants as minimal literal transversals","depends_on":["[[27-df-dual]]","[[27-df-dnf]]","[[27-df-litset]]","[[27-df-piset]]"],"local_review_status":"formalization-audited-from-supplied-text; source-not-rechecked"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Boolean Functions: Theory, Algorithms, and Applications"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"27"},{"key":"label","html":"27-thm-dualtransversal"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>27-thm-dualtransversal</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-dualtransversal — Dual prime implicants as minimal literal transversals"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"b491e41297256b44\" href=\"?note=b491e41297256b44\" title=\"27-df-dual\">27-df-dual</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"0b618255959ff4bc\" href=\"?note=0b618255959ff4bc\" title=\"27-df-dnf\">27-df-dnf</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"8311e93eaac6c631\" href=\"?note=8311e93eaac6c631\" title=\"27-df-litset\">27-df-litset</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"3e2ce4e4d23a0ce2\" href=\"?note=3e2ce4e4d23a0ce2\" title=\"27-df-piset\">27-df-piset</a></span></div>"},{"key":"local_review_status","html":"formalization-audited-from-supplied-text; source-not-rechecked"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\mathbb N\">\\(n\\in\\mathbb N\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"[n]=\\{1,\\ldots,n\\}\">\\([n]=\\{1,\\ldots,n\\}\\)</span>; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb B=\\{0,1\\}\">\\(\\mathbb B=\\{0,1\\}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n=\\mathbb B^{\\mathbb B^n}\">\\(\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n=\\mathbb B^{\\mathbb B^n}\\)</span>, as in <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"5d10aed668d85817\" href=\"?note=5d10aed668d85817\" title=\"27-df-boolfunc\">27-df-boolfunc</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"x_i(a)=a_i\">\\(x_i(a)=a_i\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\bar x_i(a)=1-a_i\">\\(\\bar x_i(a)=1-a_i\\)</span> for <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"i\\in[n]\">\\(i\\in[n]\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"a\\in\\mathbb B^n\">\\(a\\in\\mathbb B^n\\)</span>; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Lit}_n\">\\(\\mathrm{Lit}_n\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Term}_n\">\\(\\mathrm{Term}_n\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T_L\">\\(T_L\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Lits}\">\\(\\mathrm{Lits}\\)</span> are as in <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"8311e93eaac6c631\" href=\"?note=8311e93eaac6c631\" title=\"27-df-litset\">27-df-litset</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{DNF}_n\">\\(\\mathrm{DNF}_n\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{EvalDNF}_n:\\mathrm{DNF}_n\\to\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n\">\\(\\mathrm{EvalDNF}_n:\\mathrm{DNF}_n\\to\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n\\)</span> are as in <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"0b618255959ff4bc\" href=\"?note=0b618255959ff4bc\" title=\"27-df-dnf\">27-df-dnf</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"D\\in\\mathrm{DNF}_n\">\\(D\\in\\mathrm{DNF}_n\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\\in\\mathrm{ConsLit}_n\">\\(L\\in\\mathrm{ConsLit}_n\\)</span>; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Dual}_n\">\\(\\mathrm{Dual}_n\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PI}\">\\(\\mathrm{PI}\\)</span> are defined in <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"b491e41297256b44\" href=\"?note=b491e41297256b44\" title=\"27-df-dual\">27-df-dual</a> and <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"3e2ce4e4d23a0ce2\" href=\"?note=3e2ce4e4d23a0ce2\" title=\"27-df-piset\">27-df-piset</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"T_L\\in\\mathrm{PI}(\\mathrm{Dual}_n(\\mathrm{EvalDNF}_n(D)))\\;\\leftrightarrow\\;\\left(\\forall T\\in D\\;(L\\cap\\mathrm{Lits}(T)\\ne\\varnothing)\\land\\forall K\\subsetneq L\\;\\exists T\\in D\\;(K\\cap\\mathrm{Lits}(T)=\\varnothing)\\right).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[T_L\\in\\mathrm{PI}(\\mathrm{Dual}_n(\\mathrm{EvalDNF}_n(D)))\\;\\leftrightarrow\\;\\left(\\forall T\\in D\\;(L\\cap\\mathrm{Lits}(T)\\ne\\varnothing)\\land\\forall K\\subsetneq L\\;\\exists T\\in D\\;(K\\cap\\mathrm{Lits}(T)=\\varnothing)\\right).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>来源：Crama–Hammer (2011), §4.1.2, Theorem 4.7，印刷页 170，PDF 第 194 页（从 1 计数）。 已核对证明：对偶 DNF 的 CNF 中，项 T_L 蕴涵每个子句恰等价于文字集击中每个输入项；consistent L 的任何子集仍 consistent，最小性正好对应素性。极小 transversal 必须限制为一致文字集，一般带正负文字的超图 transversal 不能无条件当成项。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"27-df-dual","status":"resolved","id":"b491e41297256b44","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[27-df-dual]]","embed":false},{"target":"27-df-dnf","status":"resolved","id":"0b618255959ff4bc","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[27-df-dnf]]","embed":false},{"target":"27-df-litset","status":"resolved","id":"8311e93eaac6c631","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[27-df-litset]]","embed":false},{"target":"27-df-piset","status":"resolved","id":"3e2ce4e4d23a0ce2","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[27-df-piset]]","embed":false},{"target":"27-df-boolfunc","status":"resolved","id":"5d10aed668d85817","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$n\\in\\mathbb N$, $[n]=\\{1,\\ldots,n\\}$; $\\mathbb B=\\{0,1\\}$ and $\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n=\\mathbb B^{\\mathbb B^n}$, as in [[27-df-boolfunc]].","embed":false},{"target":"27-df-litset","status":"resolved","id":"8311e93eaac6c631","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$x_i(a)=a_i$, $\\bar x_i(a)=1-a_i$ for $i\\in[n]$, $a\\in\\mathbb B^n$; $\\mathrm{Lit}_n$, $\\mathrm{Term}_n$, $T_L$ and $\\mathrm{Lits}$ are as in [[27-df-litset]].","embed":false},{"target":"27-df-dnf","status":"resolved","id":"0b618255959ff4bc","anchor":"ref-7","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{DNF}_n$ and $\\mathrm{EvalDNF}_n:\\mathrm{DNF}_n\\to\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n$ are as in [[27-df-dnf]].","embed":false},{"target":"27-df-dual","status":"resolved","id":"b491e41297256b44","anchor":"ref-8","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$D\\in\\mathrm{DNF}_n$, $L\\in\\mathrm{ConsLit}_n$; $\\mathrm{Dual}_n$ and $\\mathrm{PI}$ are defined in [[27-df-dual]] and [[27-df-piset]].","embed":false},{"target":"27-df-piset","status":"resolved","id":"3e2ce4e4d23a0ce2","anchor":"ref-9","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$D\\in\\mathrm{DNF}_n$, $L\\in\\mathrm{ConsLit}_n$; $\\mathrm{Dual}_n$ and $\\mathrm{PI}$ are defined in [[27-df-dual]] and [[27-df-piset]].","embed":false}],"attachments":[],"math":[{"tex":"n\\in\\mathbb N","display":false},{"tex":"[n]=\\{1,\\ldots,n\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb B=\\{0,1\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n=\\mathbb B^{\\mathbb B^n}","display":false},{"tex":"x_i(a)=a_i","display":false},{"tex":"\\bar x_i(a)=1-a_i","display":false},{"tex":"i\\in[n]","display":false},{"tex":"a\\in\\mathbb B^n","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Lit}_n","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Term}_n","display":false},{"tex":"T_L","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Lits}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{DNF}_n","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{EvalDNF}_n:\\mathrm{DNF}_n\\to\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n","display":false},{"tex":"D\\in\\mathrm{DNF}_n","display":false},{"tex":"L\\in\\mathrm{ConsLit}_n","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Dual}_n","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{PI}","display":false},{"tex":"T_L\\in\\mathrm{PI}(\\mathrm{Dual}_n(\\mathrm{EvalDNF}_n(D)))\\;\\leftrightarrow\\;\\left(\\forall T\\in D\\;(L\\cap\\mathrm{Lits}(T)\\ne\\varnothing)\\land\\forall K\\subsetneq L\\;\\exists T\\in D\\;(K\\cap\\mathrm{Lits}(T)=\\varnothing)\\right).","display":true}],"bytes":1757,"backlinks":[{"id":"5244dbb38da17b8a","anchor":"ref-411","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[27-thm-dualtransversal|thm-dualtransversal — Dual prime implicants as minimal literal transversals]]"},{"id":"e12a91afc1e6fbc6","anchor":"ref-4","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""}],"outgoing":["b491e41297256b44","0b618255959ff4bc","8311e93eaac6c631","3e2ce4e4d23a0ce2","5d10aed668d85817"]}